  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "rxru3Hlxh4n3"
   },
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## Section 5 — Measure a starting point BEFORE any training (to prove learning)\n",
    "\n",
    "A single number from the finished model cannot show that the model *learned* — you need something to\n",
    "compare against. So before any training, we take the **off-the-shelf YOLOv8n** (the same standard\n",
    "pretrained weights our own training starts from) and measure how well it already does on our\n",
    "validation photos, scored against the same boxes Florence-2 produced.\n",
    "\n",
    "Out of the box, that model predicts a long list of generic object types. We keep only the ones that\n",
    "match our project and translate them into our two classes:\n",
    "\n",
    "- its `person` → **person**\n",
    "- its `bicycle`, `car`, `motorcycle`, `bus`, `truck` → **vehicle**\n",
    "\n",
    "Everything else it predicts is ignored. We score with **torchmetrics `MeanAveragePrecision`**, a\n",
    "well-tested, independent measurement. This becomes the first row of the comparison table, so \"raw\"\n",
    "and \"augmented\" can be read as real improvements over a known starting point.\n",
    "\n",
    "> To be clear: this pretrained model is only **run once for measurement**. It contributes nothing to\n",
    "> our dataset, and our models are trained **only** on our Florence-2-labelled Flickr photos.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "yuJ0YFh3h4n3",
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
    },
    "outputId": "8d65fbbf-6b62-47f5-f2a8-333dd60d2e86"
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "Creating new Ultralytics Settings v0.0.6 file ✅ \n",
      "View Ultralytics Settings with 'yolo settings' or at '/root/.config/Ultralytics/settings.json'\n",
      "Update Settings with 'yolo settings key=value', i.e. 'yolo settings runs_dir=path/to/dir'. For help see https://docs.ultralytics.com/quickstart/#ultralytics-settings.\n",
      "218 validation photos to score against.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Tools for measuring detection quality.\n",
    "from ultralytics import YOLO\n",
    "from torchmetrics.detection.mean_ap import MeanAveragePrecision\n",
    "\n",
    "VAL_IMG_DIR = DATASET_DIR / \"images\" / \"val\"\n",
    "VAL_LBL_DIR = DATASET_DIR / \"labels\" / \"val\"\n",
    "val_images = sorted(p for p in VAL_IMG_DIR.iterdir()\n",
    "                    if p.suffix.lower() in (\".jpg\", \".jpeg\", \".png\"))\n",
    "print(f\"{len(val_images)} validation photos to score against.\")\n",
    "\n",
    "def load_ground_truth(image_path):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Read our YOLO label file and return the true boxes as pixel corners plus their class ids.\"\"\"\n",
    "    W, H = Image.open(image_path).size\n",
    "    label_file = VAL_LBL_DIR / f\"{image_path.stem}.txt\"\n",
    "    boxes, labels = [], []\n",
    "    if label_file.exists():\n",
    "        for line in label_file.read_text().splitlines():\n",
    "            if not line.strip():\n",
    "                continue\n",
    "            c, xc, yc, w, h = map(float, line.split())\n",
    "            boxes.append([(xc - w / 2) * W, (yc - h / 2) * H,\n",
    "                          (xc + w / 2) * W, (yc + h / 2) * H])\n",
    "            labels.append(int(c))\n",
    "    return (torch.tensor(boxes, dtype=torch.float32).reshape(-1, 4),\n",
    "            torch.tensor(labels, dtype=torch.int64))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "qlRUOdq8h4n4"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# The off-the-shelf model numbers its generic classes in a standard order.\n",
    "# This small table translates the ones we care about into our two project classes\n",
    "# (used ONLY for the before-training baseline measurement).\n",
    "PRETRAINED_TO_PROJECT = {0: PERSON_ID, 1: VEHICLE_ID, 2: VEHICLE_ID, 3: VEHICLE_ID, 5: VEHICLE_ID, 7: VEHICLE_ID}\n",
    "\n",
    "def evaluate_map(model, remap=None, conf=0.25):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Run a model on the validation photos and return standard detection scores (mAP etc.).\n",
    "    `remap` optionally converts model class numbers into our class numbers (for the baseline).\"\"\"\n",
    "    metric = MeanAveragePrecision(box_format=\"xyxy\", iou_type=\"bbox\", class_metrics=True)\n",
    "    for image_path in val_images:\n",
    "        gt_boxes, gt_labels = load_ground_truth(image_path)\n",
    "        result = model.predict(source=str(image_path), conf=conf, verbose=False, device=DEVICE)[0]\n",
    "\n",
    "        pred_boxes, pred_scores, pred_labels = [], [], []\n",
    "        if result.boxes is not None and len(result.boxes) > 0:\n",
    "            xyxy = result.boxes.xyxy.cpu().numpy()\n",
    "            scores = result.boxes.conf.cpu().numpy()\n",
    "            classes = result.boxes.cls.cpu().numpy().astype(int)\n",
    "            for box, score, cls in zip(xyxy, scores, classes):\n",
    "                if remap is not None:\n",
    "                    if cls not in remap:\n",
    "                        continue                 # ignore object types outside our project\n",
    "                    cls = remap[cls]\n",
    "                pred_boxes.append(box.tolist()); pred_scores.append(float(score)); pred_labels.append(int(cls))\n",
    "\n",
    "        preds = [{\"boxes\": torch.tensor(pred_boxes, dtype=torch.float32).reshape(-1, 4),\n",
    "                  \"scores\": torch.tensor(pred_scores, dtype=torch.float32).reshape(-1),\n",
    "                  \"labels\": torch.tensor(pred_labels, dtype=torch.int64).reshape(-1)}]\n",
    "        target = [{\"boxes\": gt_boxes, \"labels\": gt_labels}]\n",
    "        metric.update(preds, target)\n",
    "    return metric.compute()\n",
    "\n",
    "def read_map_fields(m):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Pull out the few numbers we report from the torchmetrics result.\"\"\"\n",
    "    per_class = {}\n",
    "    if \"map_per_class\" in m and m[\"map_per_class\"].numel() > 0:\n",
    "        for cid, val in zip(m[\"classes\"].tolist(), m[\"map_per_class\"].tolist()):\n",
    "            per_class[int(cid)] = float(val)\n",
    "    return {\"mAP50\": float(m[\"map_50\"]), \"mAP50-95\": float(m[\"map\"]),\n",
    "            \"person_map\": per_class.get(PERSON_ID, float(\"nan\")),\n",
    "            \"vehicle_map\": per_class.get(VEHICLE_ID, float(\"nan\"))}"
   ]
  },
